Bluetooth: set the random address while extended advertising

set_random_addr() defers a new random address while advertising, so an
advertising instance keeps the address it uses. Extended advertising sets
have addresses of their own (LE Set Advertising Set Random Address), but
the address is deferred all the same; an active scan, whose own address
is random, then finds none set and is refused with Invalid HCI Command
Parameters for as long as an advertising set runs (on the AIC8800D: no LE
scan while BluFi advertises). Defer only for legacy advertising.

--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_request.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_request.c
@@ -2460,8 +2460,13 @@
 	 *
 	 * In this kind of scenario skip the update and let the random
 	 * address be updated at the next cycle.
+	 *
+	 * Extended advertising sets have addresses of their own (LE Set
+	 * Advertising Set Random Address), so advertising does not hold this
+	 * one; deferring it would leave an active scan with no random address,
+	 * refused with Invalid HCI Command Parameters.
 	 */
-	if (hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_ADV) ||
+	if ((!ext_adv_capable(hdev) && hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_ADV)) ||
 	    hci_lookup_le_connect(hdev)) {
 		BT_DBG("Deferring random address update");
 		hci_dev_set_flag(hdev, HCI_RPA_EXPIRED);
